  "market_context": "Uptrend on NAS100 with price making higher highs and higher lows, approaching a strong resistance zone near 15466–15467. RSI showed an early regular divergence (price HH, RSI LH) but remained within the 70/30 range.",
  "key_observation": "An early regular divergence appeared where price made a higher high while RSI made a lower high, but the analyst deliberately skipped it because RSI had not yet exited and re-entered the 70/30 range.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a regular divergence on the 15-minute NAS100 chart: price formed a higher high while RSI formed a lower high.",
    "Step 2: Checked RSI position relative to the 70/30 range and observed that RSI had not yet exited the overbought zone (remained below 70) before the divergence occurred.",
    "Step 3: Applied the 'secret sauce' filter: waited for RSI to first move above 70 (overbought), then pull back into the 70–30 range before considering any trade entry.",
    "Step 4: Concluded the early divergence was a false signal and should be ignored without the RSI range exit/re-entry confirmation."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Early divergences without RSI exiting and re-entering the 70/30 range are unreliable; the secret sauce filter prevents premature entries by requiring momentum confirmation via RSI range behavior.",
